Use the system tree-sitter runtime instead of building one at dune time.

The tree-sitter.bindings flags rule depended on %{project_root}/tree-sitter-out,
a dune rule that downloads tree-sitter 0.26.3 from the network
(core/scripts/download-tree-sitter) and builds it. conda-forge builds are
offline and provide tree-sitter, so drop that dependency and let
config/discover.exe find tree-sitter through the ambient PKG_CONFIG_PATH.
discover.exe queries the pkg-config package named "tree-sitter" (the .pc file
shipped by the conda-forge libtree-sitter package). Upstream pins 0.26.3
(core/tree-sitter-version). The vendored parser.c files all use
LANGUAGE_VERSION 14, which older runtimes (ABI 14 supported) also accept; the
C API used by bindings.c is the only other constraint.

--- a/libs/ocaml-tree-sitter-semgrep/core/src/bindings/lib/dune
+++ b/libs/ocaml-tree-sitter-semgrep/core/src/bindings/lib/dune
@@ -23,19 +23,13 @@
 
 (rule
  (targets c_flags.sexp c_library_flags.sexp)
- (deps (:tree-sitter-prefix %{project_root}/tree-sitter-out))
  (action
-  ; Neutralize PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR for this query: on Windows the mingw
-  ; pkg-config otherwise prepends its sysroot to tree-sitter.pc's absolute C:/
-  ; include/lib paths, producing a broken "-I<sysroot>C:/..." fragment that hides
-  ; <tree_sitter/api.h>.
+  ; Use the system (conda) tree-sitter found through the ambient
+  ; PKG_CONFIG_PATH instead of downloading and building one into tree-sitter-out.
   (setenv
    PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR
    ""
-   (setenv
-    PKG_CONFIG_PATH
-    "%{tree-sitter-prefix}/lib/pkgconfig:%{env:PKG_CONFIG_PATH=}"
-    (run ./config/discover.exe)))))
+   (run ./config/discover.exe))))
 
 ; atdgen preprocessing for json support
 
